From: Uke Linux contributors
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: wcd939x: preserve errors from platform data providers

GPIO and regulator providers can return -EPROBE_DEFER while LPASS clocks
and pins are still registering. Replacing that error with -EINVAL stops
the deferred retry and leaves the codec unavailable. Preserve the original
error, including permanent configuration failures.

--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x.c
@@ -3555,10 +3555,8 @@ static int wcd939x_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	wcd939x->common.max_bias = 4;
 
 	ret = wcd939x_populate_dt_data(wcd939x, dev);
-	if (ret) {
-		dev_err(dev, "%s: Fail to obtain platform data\n", __func__);
-		return -EINVAL;
-	}
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
 
 	ret = wcd939x_add_typec(wcd939x, dev);
 	if (ret)
